 "pdf": "ads8364.pdf",
 "pages": "p.2 (ROC), p.4 (digital specs, supplies, twos complement), p.5 (pinout, pin descriptions), p.6 (timing: tCONV 3.2 us, tD6 60 ns at BVDD 3 V), p.12 (CLK, RESET), p.13 (EOC, FD, Table II, start of conversion, reading data), p.14 (BYTE, ADD, software control), p.15-16 (Tables III-V)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs and the internal 2.5 V reference (REFOUT never driven): every conversion returns the 0 V differential code 0000h",
  "only HOLDA starts a conversion (the schema has one convst pin); HOLDB and HOLDC, simultaneous holds and the ignoring of further HOLD pulses until the conversion is done are not modeled",
  "the six output registers, cycle mode (A2 A1 A0 = 110) and FIFO mode (111) with their read sequencing, the ADD = 1 address/data-valid word (1000 0000 0000 dv a2 a1 a0 before the data), the empty-FIFO zero word and the FD (first data) output: every address returns the 0 V result",
  "BYTE = 1 (8-bit reads: low byte then high byte on successive RD pulses) is not modeled (stateful per-read sequencing)",
  "software control (Table V): the configuration word is stored in an internal register but its ADD/A2-A0 bits do not change reads (the bus address pins select); the control word (RESET, HOLDA, HOLDB, HOLDC) has no action because this datasheet does not state the bit polarity; data-bus bits DB15-DB8 are don't-care in a write",
  "the conversion runs on the external CLK (16.5 clocks to the output latch, 20 clocks per conversion, fCLK max 5 MHz); the model uses the 3.2 us maximum conversion time; EOC is a half-clock low pulse (100 ns at 5 MHz); latch delays while a read is in progress are not modeled",
  "bus float delay is not specified (tDf 0); DVDD (4.75-5.25 V) is the internal logic supply, the vcc range is BVDD's"
 ],
 "variants": "ADS8364Y (only grade); the ADS8365 is a later, separate datasheet with NAP, power-down and a selectable output format",
